  message: "Resolved by emission-parity:F1 / G2 gate (PR #4202, tests/test_emission_parity_matrix.py). WI-rubip core concern — substrate-derived matrices at n<=9 cannot separate analyzer-gap from construct-absent — is fixed by the gate INJECTED uniform fixtures: every language fixture provably contains a call and an import, so an empty edge_calls/edge_imports cell is unambiguously an analyzer gap. Live: edge_calls present for all 8 langs; edge_imports present for 7 (java is the documented INV-gojit hole). The methodology WI-rubip recommended (injected fixtures, never self-substrate counts) is now the standing gate."  # f678
